        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a6781fe3-db92-56a6-8360-d18acfcaf8bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Bank of British North America, British Bank of North America\n- Places: London, England; Toronto; Montreal; Quebec City; Saint John, New Brunswick; Halifax; St. John's, Newfoundland; Bay of Fundy; New Brunswick\n- Products: Royal Charter\n- Buildings: Bank of British North America Building\n- Concepts: Italianate style\n- Topics: Population\n\nFacts:\n- The Bank of British North America was founded in 1836 in London, England by a Royal Charter.\n- The Bank of British North America had offices in Toronto, Montreal, Quebec City, Saint John, New Brunswick, Halifax, and St. John's, Newfoundland.\n- The Bank of British North America Building was constructed in 1849 in the Italianate style for the British Bank of North America, described as Newfoundland's first commercial bank.\n- Saint John is a port city on the Bay of Fundy in the Canadian province of New Brunswick.\n- In 2016, Saint John had a population of 67,575 and an area of 315.82 square kilometres.\n- In 2016, after a decades-long decline, Saint John fell from the most populous city in New Brunswick to the second most populous city in the province for the first time.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
